cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EVSAE in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "EVSAE: Ear-Voice Span Analysis and Editing"
abstract: >-
  Open-source desktop application that automates Ear-Voice Span (EVS)
  measurement for simultaneous interpreting research: deterministic speech
  recognition with word-level timestamps, sentence re-segmentation, causal
  dynamic time warping alignment of source and interpreter utterances, EVS
  computation and categorisation, and a confidence-triaged verification
  interface.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/diks15/evsae"
keywords:
  - Ear-Voice Span
  - simultaneous interpreting
  - automatic speech recognition
  - dynamic time warping
  - human-in-the-loop annotation
  - corpus-based interpreting studies
authors:
  # TODO: replace with the real author list, in the order used in the article.
  - family-names: "<Family name 1>"
    given-names: "<Given name 1>"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Language and Literature Education, Universitas Pendidikan Indonesia"
